    "title": "Lesson 31: Loop Controls: break to Terminate & continue to Skip",
    "slug": "python-lesson-31-loop-controls-break-to-terminate-continue-to-skip",
    "category": "programming",
    "track": "python",
    "track_name": "Python Path",
    "category_name": "Python Programming",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "summary": "Harness loop control statements to break out immediately or skip to the next iteration.",
    "content": "# Lesson 31: Loop Controls: break to Terminate & continue to Skip\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 31** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Python Curriculum. In this lesson, you will master **Loop Controls: break to Terminate & continue to Skip** with practical explanations and live code examples.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concepts & Theoretical Background\nHarness loop control statements to break out immediately or skip to the next iteration.\n\nIn modern software development and automation, mastering this concept gives you the ability to write clean, maintainable, and high-performance Python code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical Code Implementation\nStudy the code snippet below and run it in the **Python Code Lab**:\n\n```python\nfor num in range(1, 10):\n    if num % 2 == 0:\n        continue  # Skip even numbers\n    if num == 7:\n        print(\"Target 7 found, halting loop!\")\n        break\n    print(f\"Processing odd: {num}\")\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro Tip for Python Developers**: Always adhere to PEP 8 standards and keep your code expressive and readable. In Python, explicit is better than implicit!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nTake your knowledge to the next level by completing this coding challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Iterate through a list of filenames, skip any file ending with .tmp, and stop when finding error.log.\n2. Open the **Interactive Python Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your solution, verify the output terminal, and observe how your code behaves!\n",
    "tags": "Python, Lesson 31, Programming, Intermediate",
