    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "summary": "Perform Venn diagram operations on sets to compare datasets with mathematical rigor.",
    "content": "# Lesson 40: Set Operations: Union (|), Intersection (&), Difference (-)\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 40** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Python Curriculum. In this lesson, you will master **Set Operations: Union (|), Intersection (&), Difference (-)** with practical explanations and live code examples.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concepts & Theoretical Background\nPerform Venn diagram operations on sets to compare datasets with mathematical rigor.\n\nIn modern software development and automation, mastering this concept gives you the ability to write clean, maintainable, and high-performance Python code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical Code Implementation\nStudy the code snippet below and run it in the **Python Code Lab**:\n\n```python\npython_students = {\"Sara\", \"Mohammed\", \"Khalid\", \"Fatima\"}\nexcel_students = {\"Fatima\", \"Zaid\", \"Mohammed\", \"Noura\"}\n\nprint(\"Both Courses (&):\", python_students & excel_students)\nprint(\"Either Course (|):\", python_students | excel_students)\nprint(\"Python Only (-):\", python_students - excel_students)\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro Tip for Python Developers**: Always adhere to PEP 8 standards and keep your code expressive and readable. In Python, explicit is better than implicit!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nTake your knowledge to the next level by completing this coding challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Find common skills between a job posting requirements set and a candidate's resume skills set.\n2. Open the **Interactive Python Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your solution, verify the output terminal, and observe how your code behaves!\n",
