    "summary": "Combine strings, random choices, conditionals, and functions to create strong passwords.",
    "content": "# Lesson 60: Mini-Project 3: Secure Password Generator with Entropy Scorer\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 60** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Python Curriculum. In this lesson, you will master **Mini-Project 3: Secure Password Generator with Entropy Scorer** with practical explanations and live code examples.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concepts & Theoretical Background\nCombine strings, random choices, conditionals, and functions to create strong passwords.\n\nIn modern software development and automation, mastering this concept gives you the ability to write clean, maintainable, and high-performance Python code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical Code Implementation\nStudy the code snippet below and run it in the **Python Code Lab**:\n\n```python\nimport random\nimport string\n\ndef generate_password(length=12, include_special=True):\n    chars = string.ascii_letters + string.digits\n    if include_special:\n        chars += \"!@#$%^&*\"\n    return \"\".join(random.choice(chars) for _ in range(length))\n\npwd = generate_password(16)\nprint(f\"Generated Password: {pwd} (Length: {len(pwd)})\")\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro Tip for Python Developers**: Always adhere to PEP 8 standards and keep your code expressive and readable. In Python, explicit is better than implicit!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nTake your knowledge to the next level by completing this coding challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Add validation to ensure the generated password contains at least one uppercase letter, one digit, and one symbol.\n2. Open the **Interactive Python Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your solution, verify the output terminal, and observe how your code behaves!\n",
