    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "summary": "Initialize object state automatically during instantiation with the constructor.",
    "content": "# Lesson 77: The __init__() Constructor & The self Parameter\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 77** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Python Curriculum. In this lesson, you will master **The __init__() Constructor & The self Parameter** with practical explanations and live code examples.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concepts & Theoretical Background\nInitialize object state automatically during instantiation with the constructor.\n\nIn modern software development and automation, mastering this concept gives you the ability to write clean, maintainable, and high-performance Python code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical Code Implementation\nStudy the code snippet below and run it in the **Python Code Lab**:\n\n```python\nclass Course:\n    def __init__(self, title, code, instructor):\n        self.title = title\n        self.code = code\n        self.instructor = instructor\n        self.enrolled_students = []\n\nc = Course(\"Python Automation\", \"PY-101\", \"Mohammed Bargisy\")\nprint(f\"Course: {c.title} ({c.code}) - Taught by {c.instructor}\")\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro Tip for Python Developers**: Always adhere to PEP 8 standards and keep your code expressive and readable. In Python, explicit is better than implicit!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nTake your knowledge to the next level by completing this coding challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Design a BankAccount class with __init__ taking account_holder and starting_balance.\n2. Open the **Interactive Python Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your solution, verify the output terminal, and observe how your code behaves!\n",
