    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "summary": "Inherit common attributes and methods from parent classes to create clean hierarchies.",
    "content": "# Lesson 83: Class Inheritance: Extending Base Classes to Eliminate Duplication\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 83** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Python Curriculum. In this lesson, you will master **Class Inheritance: Extending Base Classes to Eliminate Duplication** with practical explanations and live code examples.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concepts & Theoretical Background\nInherit common attributes and methods from parent classes to create clean hierarchies.\n\nIn modern software development and automation, mastering this concept gives you the ability to write clean, maintainable, and high-performance Python code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical Code Implementation\nStudy the code snippet below and run it in the **Python Code Lab**:\n\n```python\nclass Person:\n    def __init__(self, name, national_id):\n        self.name = name\n        self.national_id = national_id\n\n    def introduce(self):\n        return f\"Hi, I am {self.name}.\"\n\nclass Instructor(Person):\n    def __init__(self, name, national_id, subject):\n        super().__init__(name, national_id) # Call parent __init__\n        self.subject = subject\n\ninst = Instructor(\"Mohammed Bargisy\", \"ID-992\", \"Python & Excel\")\nprint(inst.introduce())\nprint(\"Teaching Subject:\", inst.subject)\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro Tip for Python Developers**: Always adhere to PEP 8 standards and keep your code expressive and readable. In Python, explicit is better than implicit!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nTake your knowledge to the next level by completing this coding challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Create a base Vehicle class and derived ElectricCar class with a battery_capacity attribute.\n2. Open the **Interactive Python Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your solution, verify the output terminal, and observe how your code behaves!\n",
    "tags": "Python, Lesson 83, Programming, Advanced",
