    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "summary": "Write flexible functions that accept any object exposing the required method interface.",
    "content": "# Lesson 85: Polymorphism & Duck Typing: 'If it quacks like a duck...'\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 85** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Python Curriculum. In this lesson, you will master **Polymorphism & Duck Typing: 'If it quacks like a duck...'** with practical explanations and live code examples.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concepts & Theoretical Background\nWrite flexible functions that accept any object exposing the required method interface.\n\nIn modern software development and automation, mastering this concept gives you the ability to write clean, maintainable, and high-performance Python code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical Code Implementation\nStudy the code snippet below and run it in the **Python Code Lab**:\n\n```python\nclass PDFReport:\n    def render(self): return \"Rendering PDF vector document...\"\n\nclass ExcelReport:\n    def render(self): return \"Generating Excel XLSX spreadsheet...\"\n\ndef export_document(report):\n    # Duck typing: doesn't care about inheritance, just calls render()\n    print(\"Export:\", report.render())\n\nexport_document(PDFReport())\nexport_document(ExcelReport())\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro Tip for Python Developers**: Always adhere to PEP 8 standards and keep your code expressive and readable. In Python, explicit is better than implicit!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nTake your knowledge to the next level by completing this coding challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Write a process_payment(payment_gateway) function that works with PayPal, Stripe, and BankWire classes.\n2. Open the **Interactive Python Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your solution, verify the output terminal, and observe how your code behaves!\n",
