    "difficulty": "Advanced",
    "summary": "Produce sequence values on demand without storing millions of items in memory.",
    "content": "# Lesson 90: Generators & The yield Keyword: Memory-Efficient Data Streams\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 90** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Python Curriculum. In this lesson, you will master **Generators & The yield Keyword: Memory-Efficient Data Streams** with practical explanations and live code examples.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concepts & Theoretical Background\nProduce sequence values on demand without storing millions of items in memory.\n\nIn modern software development and automation, mastering this concept gives you the ability to write clean, maintainable, and high-performance Python code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical Code Implementation\nStudy the code snippet below and run it in the **Python Code Lab**:\n\n```python\ndef infinite_counter(start=1):\n    while True:\n        yield start\n        start += 1\n\ngen = infinite_counter(100)\nprint(next(gen)) # 100\nprint(next(gen)) # 101\nprint(next(gen)) # 102\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro Tip for Python Developers**: Always adhere to PEP 8 standards and keep your code expressive and readable. In Python, explicit is better than implicit!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nTake your knowledge to the next level by completing this coding challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Write a generator fibonacci_sequence(limit) that yields Fibonacci numbers up to a specified limit.\n2. Open the **Interactive Python Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your solution, verify the output terminal, and observe how your code behaves!\n",
