    "content": "# Lesson 100: Capstone Project: Automated Data Cleaning & Report Generation Engine\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 100** of the Bargisy eSchool Complete Python Curriculum. In this lesson, you will master **Capstone Project: Automated Data Cleaning & Report Generation Engine** with practical explanations and live code examples.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Concepts & Theoretical Background\nSynthesize everything: functions, file I/O, OOP, error handling, and datetime into a complete automation tool.\n\nIn modern software development and automation, mastering this concept gives you the ability to write clean, maintainable, and high-performance Python code.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical Code Implementation\nStudy the code snippet below and run it in the **Python Code Lab**:\n\n```python\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\nclass ReportGenerator:\n    def __init__(self, school_name=\"Bargisy eSchool\"):\n        self.school_name = school_name\n        self.records = []\n\n    def add_record(self, student_name, track, score):\n        self.records.append({\n            \"name\": student_name,\n            \"track\": track,\n            \"score\": score,\n            \"passed\": score >= 70\n        })\n\n    def generate_summary(self):\n        total = len(self.records)\n        if total == 0:\n            return \"No records to summarize.\"\n        avg_score = sum(r[\"score\"] for r in self.records) / total\n        pass_count = sum(1 for r in self.records if r[\"passed\"])\n        \n        return f\"\"\"=======================================\n🎓 {self.school_name} - Official Summary Report\nDate: {datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')}\nTotal Students Processed: {total}\nAverage Score: {avg_score:.1f}%\nPass Rate: {(pass_count / total) * 100:.1f}%\n=======================================\"\"\"\n\nrep = ReportGenerator()\nrep.add_record(\"Mohammed Bargisy\", \"Python\", 98)\nrep.add_record(\"Sara Al-Harbi\", \"Front-End\", 94)\nrep.add_record(\"Khalid Al-Otaibi\", \"Python\", 88)\nprint(rep.generate_summary())\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Pro Tip for Python Developers**: Always adhere to PEP 8 standards and keep your code expressive and readable. In Python, explicit is better than implicit!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nTake your knowledge to the next level by completing this coding challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Run this capstone engine, add 5 student records across both Python and Front-End tracks, and print the official summary report!\n2. Open the **Interactive Python Lab** in Bargisy eSchool.\n3. Test your solution, verify the output terminal, and observe how your code behaves!\n",
